      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the object_metadata.py file that reads object metadata or head information from managed object storage, I will use the AWS S3 service as the concrete external provider. This is because AWS S3 is a widely used managed object storage service and has a well-documented SDK. The provider will be identifiable in the code through the use of the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python. </thinking>\n",
